<title>BELGIUM: Sabena scraps Oct 17 flights to France.</title>
<headline>Sabena scraps Oct 17 flights to France.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgian airline Sabena said on Wednesday it was cancelling all flights with destination France on October 17 because of announced strikes by civil servants there.</p>
<p>It said in a statement that in view of the action French air traffic controllers would not allow any flights to land on French soil on Thursday.</p>
<p>The strikes are aimed at government cutbacks and record unemployment.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
